Inkling-2-Mini abliterated - ingine
Copyright 2026 satellitedown

This repository contains ingine (a C++/CUDA inference engine for
Inkling-2-Mini, in native/), the abliteration tools, the abliteration file
ablation/inkling-2-mini-abliterated.safetensors, and an installer. All of it
is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE), except the
vendored dependencies listed below, which keep their own licenses.

The model weights are not part of the GitHub repository; they are
redistributed unchanged in the Hugging Face repository named below. This
license does not replace the licenses of downloaded software or model
artifacts.

Installer recipe
----------------
Adapted from the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next heretic - fngine installer:
https://github.com/satellitedown/flash-next-abliterated-fngine
The recipe has been changed to build ingine's C++/CUDA server from this
repository on the installing machine (CMake, Ninja and a private CUDA toolkit
with cuBLAS from NVIDIA's pip packages), and to download the pinned
satellitedown/Inkling-2-Mini-abliterated-ingine revision from Hugging Face.

ingine's C++ engine
-------------------
Its device, memory, weight-loading, CUDA-graph and tracing infrastructure, the
OpenAI-compatible HTTP server and the tokenizer and chat-template pipeline are
adapted from fngine (Apache License 2.0):
https://github.com/satellitedown/fngine
fngine is derived in part from Cinference (commit 383e5db,
https://github.com/satellitedown/cinference), which is derived from NInfer by
Neroued and its contributors (https://github.com/Neroued/ninfer), all under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. Adapted files carry a header of the form
"Adapted from fngine (github.com/satellitedown/fngine, Apache-2.0) for
ingine.", and files fngine took from Cinference keep their "Modified for
fngine from cinference:<path> @ 383e5db. See NOTICE." header. The model
kernels, the prefill, the DSpark drafter and the speculative decoding loop are
written for Inkling-2-Mini; the decode kernels are ports of ingine's earlier
PyTorch extension kernels.

RTX 3090 port and expert offloading (native/src/offload, branch rtx3090)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The expert-offloading design (pinned host experts with a VRAM expert cache,
a decayed-LFU adaptive tier, the GPU-to-CPU doorbell hand-off inside CUDA
graphs, the CPU worker pool's epoch-tagged claim protocol, per-core thread
placement and the CPU expert kernels' row structure and prefetching) follows
Strata, Copyright (c) 2026 Niko1221 and the Strata contributors, MIT License
(https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata; src/kernels/cpu/nvfp4_avx512.cpp,
include/strata/kernels/cpu/pool.hpp, include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp,
src/kernels/cuda/elementwise.cu, src/kernels/cuda/verify_kernels.cu), and
fngine's hot/cold expert tiers. No Strata source file is copied verbatim; the
adapted code is new and marked with references in its comments. Strata's
copyright and MIT license notice: native/src/offload/LICENSE.strata.

Image input (native/src/vision, branch rtx3090)
-----------------------------------------------
The image preprocessing and the vision tower follow Hugging Face transformers'
Inkling 2 implementation (image_processing_inkling2.py, modeling_inkling2.py,
vision_utils.py; Apache License 2.0), cross-checked against llama.cpp's
inkling2v graph and preprocessor (MIT License). The vector erf uses the
rational approximation coefficients of Eigen's / XLA's generic_fast_erf_float
(Eigen: MPL 2.0; the coefficients are numerical constants). No source file is
copied; tools/vision_reference.py is a NumPy port of the transformers code
used as a test oracle.

