Model
-----
Inkling-2-Mini: https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Mini
Thinking Machines, Apache License 2.0, revision
6e7c8248f75265bdd4fbab5273304243b5d8c2cb. Its files, including the DSpark
drafter (mtp.safetensors), are redistributed without alteration together with
the abliteration file in:
https://huggingface.co/satellitedown/Inkling-2-Mini-abliterated-ingine
The installer downloads that repository at the immutable revision and with
the per-file sizes and SHA-256 recorded in runtime-manifest.json. The
abliteration is applied by ingine at run time; no weights were retrained or
modified.

Method and references
---------------------
- Heretic (p-e-w): https://github.com/p-e-w/heretic. The search (Optuna TPE
  over a per-layer weight kernel, refusals against KL divergence) and the
  borderline-prompt and capability evaluations in tools/ follow Heretic's
  approach and eval tools; no Heretic code is included.
- Abliteration literature: refusal directions as a difference of means and
  directional ablation (Arditi et al., "Refusal in Language Models Is
  Mediated by a Single Direction", 2024), and projected abliteration
  (directions made orthogonal to the harmless mean).
- Datasets used for directions and evaluation: mlabonne/harmful_behaviors,
  mlabonne/harmless_alpaca, JailbreakBench (JBB-Behaviors), under their own
  licenses; they are downloaded by the tools, not redistributed.
- Hugging Face transformers (Apache-2.0), pull request
  https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/51050 (Inkling2Loop): the
  reference model in tools/inkling_ref.py is built on it, and ingine's model
  was checked against it.
- PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause): the abliteration tools in tools/ run on PyTorch;
  ingine does not use it.
- vLLM (Apache-2.0): ingine's DSpark speculative decoding follows vLLM's
  implementation of the drafter.
- NVIDIA: CUDA components downloaded by the installer (compiler, runtime,
  cuBLAS) retain NVIDIA's license terms.

